1
00:00:00,051 --> 00:00:02,051
(Penny:)If you really
care that much,

2
00:00:02,053 --> 00:00:04,753
(Howard:)there are apps now that'll let
you hire people to do stuff

3
00:00:04,755 --> 00:00:06,925
(Howard:)like errands and
wait in lines.

4
00:00:06,924 --> 00:00:10,094
(Stuart:)People are actually
waiting in lines as a job?

5
00:00:10,094 --> 00:00:14,494
(Stuart:)Boy, makes me feel better
about my life.

6
00:00:14,498 --> 00:00:16,498
(Howard:)Some of these guys make
over $20 an hour.

7
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:18,800
(Stuart:)And now I feel worse again.

8
00:00:21,072 --> 00:00:24,402
(Beverly:)I'm not surprised Leonard
chose to avoid picking me up.

9
00:00:24,408 --> 00:00:28,408
(Beverly:)He's battled intimacy issues
his whole life.

10
00:00:28,412 --> 00:00:31,952
(Beverly:)Does he have difficulty
maintaining erections?

11
00:00:31,949 --> 00:00:34,279
(Penny:)Wow.
(clears throat)

12
00:00:34,285 --> 00:00:36,255
(Penny:)Didn't even make it
out of the parking lot.

13
00:00:37,354 --> 00:00:38,754
(Penny:)Uh, you know what,
enough about Leonard.

14
00:00:38,756 --> 00:00:40,026
(Penny:)Let's talk about you.

15
00:00:40,024 --> 00:00:41,794
(Penny:)What would you like to
do while you're here?

16
00:00:41,792 --> 00:00:43,692
(Beverly:)Dear, I'm a psychiatrist.

17
00:00:43,694 --> 00:00:46,694
(Beverly:)You don't have to avoid having
intimate conversations with me.

18
00:00:46,697 --> 00:00:50,097
(Penny:)Well, I'd actually like
for us to be close,

19
00:00:50,101 --> 00:00:52,071
(Penny:)but maybe we start
with our favorite books

20
00:00:52,069 --> 00:00:54,669
(Penny:)and work our way up
to my husband's sex organs.

21
00:00:56,574 --> 00:00:57,874
(Beverly:)Very well.

22
00:00:57,875 --> 00:00:59,045
(Beverly:)What's the last book
you read?

